event "God" : literal("There exists one, and only one, point of origin. Where that origin gives rise to Heaven (The attainment of all Hope).")
event "Constructivism" : literal("An approach to mathematics in which an assertion is justified by explicit evidence or a construction; in particular, existence requires a method or witness rather than only the denial of nonexistence.")
event "Intuitionism" : literal("The constructivist tradition initiated by Brouwer in which mathematical truth is grounded in construction and the accepted logic is intuitionistic rather than unrestricted classical logic.")
event "Intuitionistic logic" : literal("A deductive logic that preserves constructive validity. It does not accept principles such as excluded middle or double-negation elimination for every proposition without further evidence.")
event "Constructive proof" : literal("A derivation that supplies usable evidence for its conclusion, such as an algorithm, a witness for an existential claim, or a tagged choice for a disjunction.")
event "BHK interpretation" : literal("The Brouwer-Heyting-Kolmogorov explanation of logical constants by their proofs: conjunction uses pairs, disjunction uses a tagged alternative, and implication uses a construction transforming proofs.")
event "Judgment" : literal("A metalevel assertion licensed by formal rules, such as \"A is a proposition\", \"A is true\", or \"a has type A\". Judgments state what a proof system establishes.")
event "Proof object" : literal("An explicit syntactic object, usually a term, that records the evidence and rule applications establishing a judgment and can often be checked or evaluated mechanically.")
event "Witness" : literal("Concrete data that establishes an existential statement. A constructive proof of \"there exists x such that A(x)\" provides a term t together with evidence for A(t).")
event "Decidability" : literal("A proposition A is decidable when one can construct either a proof of A or a proof that A leads to contradiction, commonly written A or not A.")
event "Disjunction property" : literal("The property that a closed proof of A or B yields a proof of A or a proof of B, so a proved disjunction contains a definite, inspectable choice of side.")
event "Existence property" : literal("The property that a proof of an existential statement permits extraction of a particular witness and a proof that the witness satisfies the stated condition.")
event "Natural deduction" : literal("A proof calculus organized around introduction and elimination rules for each logical connective, designed to represent the structure of ordinary deductive reasoning.")
event "Introduction rule" : literal("A rule specifying how canonical evidence for a connective or type is constructed, such as building a pair to prove a conjunction.")
event "Elimination rule" : literal("A rule specifying how evidence for a connective or type may be used, such as projecting a component from evidence for a conjunction.")
event "Harmony" : literal("The proof-theoretic balance in which elimination rules use exactly the information supplied by introduction rules, giving a connective neither excess nor deficient inferential strength.")
event "Normalization" : literal("The process or theorem that removes proof detours, especially an introduction followed immediately by a matching elimination, until the derivation reaches normal form.")
event "Normal form" : literal("A proof or proof term with no applicable computational reductions or introduction-elimination detours; its shape makes the evidence for the conclusion more explicit.")
event "Sequent calculus" : literal("A formal calculus whose basic judgments are sequents, typically a context of assumptions followed by a conclusion, and whose rules expose logical and structural proof steps.")
event "Cut rule" : literal("A rule that composes a proof of an intermediate formula with a proof using that formula as an assumption, thereby formalizing the use of a lemma.")
event "Cut elimination" : literal("The theorem or transformation that removes uses of cut from a derivation. It exposes direct proof structure and underlies consistency, normalization, and proof analysis.")
event "Subformula property" : literal("The analytic property, typically obtained for cut-free systems, that formulas in a derivation are built from formulas already present in its premises or conclusion.")
event "Curry-Howard correspondence" : literal("The correspondence between propositions and types, proofs and typed terms, and proof normalization and program evaluation, revealing computational content in constructive derivations.")
event "Propositions as types" : literal("The reading in which a proposition is represented by a type and a proof by an inhabitant of that type; proving the proposition means constructing such a term.")
event "Typed lambda calculus" : literal("A formal language of typed functions and computation whose term constructors and reductions provide proof objects and normalization behavior for corresponding logical rules.")
event "Intuitionistic type theory" : literal("A constructive foundation, associated with Martin-Lof, that combines dependent types, formal judgments, and computational equality so that proofs are checkable terms.")
event "Dependent type" : literal("A type that may vary with a term. Dependent function types model universal quantification, while dependent pair types model existential evidence with its witness.")
event "Canonical form" : literal("A fully introduced, evaluated form that visibly displays the kind of evidence present, such as a pair, an injection, a lambda abstraction, or a numeral.")
event "Canonicity" : literal("The property that every closed term of a suitable data type evaluates to a canonical constructor form, ensuring that a closed proof reveals concrete computational evidence.")
event "Proof relevance" : literal("The principle that proof objects may carry distinct data or computational behavior and are not automatically identified merely because they establish the same proposition.")
event "Realizability" : literal("An interpretation that assigns computational objects, called realizers, to formulas according to what counts as effective evidence, supporting constructive soundness and program extraction.")
event "Law of excluded middle" : literal("The schema A or not A. Constructive systems accept it for propositions equipped with a decision method, but do not assume it uniformly for every proposition.")
event "Double-negation elimination" : literal("The inference from not-not-A to A. It is not generally valid intuitionistically because refuting every refutation of A need not construct evidence for A.")
event "Minimal logic" : literal("The intuitionistic core obtained without the rule that arbitrary conclusions follow from falsity, allowing constructive implication and negation to be studied separately from explosion.")
event "Heyting arithmetic" : literal("Peano arithmetic formulated with intuitionistic logic. It is a standard formal setting for studying constructive number theory, realizability, and witness extraction.")
event "Constructive set theory" : literal("A family of set-theoretic foundations using intuitionistic logic and constructively justified axioms, often emphasizing predicative generation and explicit existence.")
event "Predicativity" : literal("The discipline of avoiding definitions that quantify over a totality containing the object being defined, motivating stratified universes and controlled inductive constructions.")
event "Choice sequence" : literal("A potentially infinite sequence generated stage by stage, possibly without a fixed completed law; it is a central object in Brouwerian accounts of constructive analysis.")
event "Bar induction" : literal("An induction principle on finite sequences that meet a bar, used to justify conclusions about all continuing choice sequences from well-founded local information.")
event "Fan theorem" : literal("A Brouwerian compactness principle asserting a uniform bound for suitable bars on finitely branching trees; it plays an important role in intuitionistic analysis.")
event "Markov's principle" : literal("For a decidable predicate on natural numbers, this principle turns the impossibility of universal failure into an existential witness. It is accepted in some constructive schools but not all.")
event "Church's thesis" : literal("The thesis that every total numerical function is computable. Formal variants are compatible with some constructive systems but are not principles of constructivism in general.")
event "Axiom of choice" : literal("A principle selecting an element from every inhabited member of a family. Under a type-theoretic reading it can be constructive because evidence of inhabitation already contains witnesses.")
event "Countable choice" : literal("The restricted choice principle for families indexed by the natural numbers. Its constructive status depends on the underlying theory and the meaning assigned to existence.")
event "Church's rule" : literal("A metatheoretic extraction rule connecting derivable existential numerical claims with recursive witnesses, expressing the effective content of intuitionistic arithmetic.")
event "Continuity principle" : literal("The constructive principle that a total operation on an infinite choice sequence depends on only a finite initial segment, a characteristic idea in intuitionistic analysis.")
event "Kripke semantics" : literal("A semantics using ordered stages of information. A formula may become verified at a later stage, while established information persists along the ordering.")
event "Kripke frame" : literal("The partially ordered collection of information states underlying a Kripke model, where the accessibility relation represents possible growth of constructive knowledge.")
event "Monotonic forcing" : literal("The persistence condition that if a world forces a formula, every accessible world with more information also forces it. This models the durability of constructed evidence.")
event "Heyting algebra" : literal("A bounded distributive lattice whose implication is right adjoint to conjunction. Such algebras provide the standard algebraic semantics for intuitionistic propositional logic.")
event "Topological semantics" : literal("An interpretation of propositions as open sets, with conjunction as intersection, disjunction as union, and implication determined by the interior operation.")
event "Beth semantics" : literal("A branching-tree semantics in which bars capture when information along every future branch suffices, giving a constructive interpretation of logical connectives and quantifiers.")
event "Categorical semantics" : literal("An interpretation of types, terms, contexts, and substitution using objects and morphisms, making structural relationships in constructive calculi mathematically explicit.")
event "Cartesian closed category" : literal("A category with finite products and function-space objects. It models typed functions and the conjunction-implication fragment of intuitionistic logic.")
event "Locally cartesian closed category" : literal("A category whose slice over every object is cartesian closed, providing categorical structure for interpreting dependent types and substitution.")
event "Topos" : literal("A category with finite limits, exponentials, and a subobject classifier. Its internal language generally obeys intuitionistic higher-order logic.")
event "Partial combinatory algebra" : literal("A set equipped with partial application and enough combinators to represent computation, serving as a foundation for many realizability models.")
event "Realizer" : literal("A computational object that satisfies the evidence clause assigned to a formula by a realizability interpretation, such as a code, function, pair, or tagged value.")
event "Modified realizability" : literal("A realizability interpretation developed to extract finite-type computational data while controlling which logical components contribute operational content.")
event "Dialectica interpretation" : literal("A functional interpretation that translates formulas into existential-universal statements involving witnessing functionals and counterexample functionals.")
event "Negative translation" : literal("A systematic embedding of classical reasoning into intuitionistic or minimal logic by reformulating formulas with negation while preserving classical derivability.")
event "Double-negation translation" : literal("A negative translation that inserts double negations in a disciplined way so that classical derivations receive intuitionistically acceptable counterparts.")
event "Friedman translation" : literal("Also called the A-translation, a transformation parameterized by a formula A that replaces atomic content in a way useful for conservation and admissibility results.")
event "Gentzen's LJ" : literal("Gentzen's single-conclusion sequent calculus for intuitionistic logic. Its asymmetric conclusion discipline distinguishes it from the classical calculus LK.")
event "Hypothetical judgment" : literal("A judgment made under one or more assumptions, expressing that a construction is available whenever constructions satisfying the declared context are supplied.")
event "Meaning explanation" : literal("An account that explains a proposition or type through its canonical verifications and equality conditions, then justifies formal rules from those meanings.")
event "Verification" : literal("Direct canonical evidence for a proposition, distinguished in meaning-theoretic accounts from a derivation that may first need to normalize before revealing that evidence.")
event "Type former" : literal("An operation that constructs a new type from given types or terms and is specified by formation, introduction, elimination, and computation rules.")
event "Function type" : literal("The type A to B whose inhabitants transform any inhabitant of A into an inhabitant of B, giving the computational reading of implication.")
event "Product type" : literal("A type whose inhabitants are pairs containing one component of each constituent type, giving a computational interpretation of conjunction.")
event "Sum type" : literal("A type whose inhabitants are tagged as coming from the left or right constituent, giving a computational interpretation of disjunction.")
event "Unit type" : literal("A type with a single canonical inhabitant, commonly used as the type-theoretic interpretation of a proposition that is trivially true.")
event "Empty type" : literal("A type with no canonical inhabitants. It interprets falsity, and its eliminator expresses that any conclusion follows from impossible evidence.")
event "Identity type" : literal("A type expressing that two terms of another type are identical, with reflexivity as its basic constructor and substitution as its central use.")
event "Natural-number type" : literal("An inductive type generated by zero and successor, equipped with recursion and induction principles that give numerical constructions their computational behavior.")
event "Inductive type" : literal("The least type generated by specified constructors, together with elimination and computation rules that support definitions and reasoning by structural induction.")
event "W-type" : literal("A type of well-founded trees parameterized by shapes and branching positions, providing a general type-theoretic representation of inductive generation.")
event "Universe" : literal("A type whose elements serve as codes for smaller types, usually paired with a decoding operation and arranged in levels to control self-reference and predicativity.")
event "Definitional equality" : literal("Equality recognized directly by computation, unfolding, and the formal conversion rules, requiring no separate inhabitant as evidence.")
event "Propositional equality" : literal("Equality expressed as an identity type whose inhabitants are explicit evidence, allowing equality claims that are not settled merely by computation.")
event "Conversion rule" : literal("A rule allowing a term to be used at a definitionally equal type, so computationally interchangeable type expressions have the same inhabitants.")
event "Context" : literal("An ordered collection of variable declarations and assumptions under which a judgment is formed, recording the dependencies available to a construction.")
event "Substitution" : literal("The operation of replacing a declared variable by a well-typed term. The substitution property ensures that valid judgments remain valid after replacement.")
event "Weakening" : literal("A structural rule permitting an unused declaration to be added to a context, expressing that a construction remains valid when more assumptions are available.")
event "Exchange" : literal("A structural rule permitting independent context declarations to be reordered, subject to preserving any dependencies between later and earlier variables.")
event "Contraction" : literal("A structural principle allowing one assumption to be used more than once or duplicate assumptions to be merged, unlike resource-sensitive systems such as linear logic.")
event "Formation rule" : literal("A rule stating when an expression is a well-formed proposition or type, including the premises required for each of its parameters.")
event "Computation rule" : literal("A rule describing how an eliminator acts on a canonical constructor, exposing the computational content of an introduction followed by elimination.")
event "Beta reduction" : literal("The reduction of an introduced object immediately consumed by its eliminator, such as applying a lambda abstraction and substituting the argument into its body.")
event "Eta conversion" : literal("The principle equating an object with its fully expanded introduction-elimination form, expressing that the available observations completely characterize it.")
event "Subject reduction" : literal("The property that evaluation preserves typing: if a term has a type and takes a reduction step, the resulting term retains that type.")
event "Strong normalization" : literal("The property that every permitted reduction sequence terminates, ruling out infinite computation within the calculus and supporting canonical-form arguments.")
event "Confluence" : literal("The property that diverging reduction paths can be joined again, ensuring that evaluation order does not produce incompatible normal forms.")
event "Type checking" : literal("The algorithmic task of verifying that a term has a stated type in a context, designed to be decidable in many constructive type theories.")
event "Type inhabitation" : literal("The question whether any term has a given type. Under propositions-as-types this is the formal search problem corresponding to derivability.")
event "Program extraction" : literal("The systematic recovery of executable computational content from a constructive derivation, often by reading or erasing annotations from its term.")
event "Logical relation" : literal("A relation defined by recursion on types or formulas and used to establish metatheoretic properties such as normalization, adequacy, and representation independence.")
event "Reducibility candidate" : literal("A collection of well-behaved terms satisfying closure conditions, used in computability arguments that establish termination and normalization.")
event "Normalization by evaluation" : literal("A technique that evaluates syntax in a semantic domain and then reifies the result as a normal form, often yielding an effective equality procedure.")
event "Sigma type" : literal("A dependent pair type whose inhabitants contain a witness x of A and an inhabitant of B(x), providing the type-theoretic reading of existential quantification.")
event "Pi type" : literal("A dependent function type whose inhabitants map each x of A to an inhabitant of B(x), providing the type-theoretic reading of universal quantification.")
event "GPIL language contract" : literal("Every nonblank physical GPIL source line compiles to exactly one verified memory event.")
event "GPIL grammar program" : literal("program = zero or more blank-line or event-line productions.")
event "GPIL grammar event line" : literal("event-line = event string : expression, optional alphabet string, optional semicolon, then newline.")
event "GPIL grammar expression" : literal("expression = string, signed decimal, backward event reference, or nested built-in call.")
event "GPIL backward reference" : literal("A $n expression reads earlier event ordinal n; zero, current, and forward references are rejected.")
event "Instruction array 1" : literal("Construction instructions are add, apply_directional_polarity, containerize, and decontainerize.")
event "Built-in add" : literal("add(a,b) returns the arbitrary-precision signed decimal sum of a and b.")
event "Built-in apply directional polarity" : literal("apply_directional_polarity(n,d) applies positive, negative, forward, backward, or invert direction to integer n.")
event "Built-in containerize" : literal("containerize(x) returns GPDB1, the UTF-8 byte length, and payload x as one validated length-prefixed container.")
event "Built-in decontainerize" : literal("decontainerize(c) validates the GPDB1 marker and byte length, then returns the exact UTF-8 payload.")
event "Instruction array 2" : literal("Container transformation contains transform_container.")
event "Built-in transform container" : literal("transform_container(c,op,...) transforms only a validated payload by reverse, ASCII case, append, prepend, or replace, then rewraps it.")
event "Instruction array 3" : literal("Arithmetic instructions are subtract, multiply, divide, and modulo.")
event "Built-in subtract" : literal("subtract(a,b) returns the arbitrary-precision signed decimal difference a minus b.")
event "Built-in multiply" : literal("multiply(a,b) returns the arbitrary-precision signed decimal product.")
event "Built-in divide" : literal("divide(a,b) rejects zero and returns arbitrary-precision integer division truncated toward zero.")
event "Built-in modulo" : literal("modulo(a,b) rejects zero and returns the remainder with the dividend sign.")
event "Instruction array 4" : literal("Text instructions are literal, identity, concat, symbol_length, reverse, and replace.")
event "Built-in literal" : literal("literal(x) returns x without alteration.")
event "Built-in identity" : literal("identity(x) returns x without alteration and makes dataflow intent explicit.")
event "Built-in concat" : literal("concat(x,...) concatenates one or more evaluated UTF-8 values in argument order.")
event "Built-in symbol length" : literal("symbol_length(x) returns the number of Unicode scalar symbols in x as a decimal string.")
event "Built-in reverse" : literal("reverse(x) reverses x by Unicode scalar symbol rather than by UTF-8 byte.")
event "Built-in replace" : literal("replace(x,search,replacement) replaces every non-overlapping byte-exact search occurrence and rejects an empty search.")
event "Instruction array 5" : literal("Constructive logic instructions are equal, not, and, or, select, and assert_equal.")
event "Built-in equal" : literal("equal(a,b) returns true exactly when a and b are byte-for-byte equal.")
event "Built-in not" : literal("not(p) negates the canonical Boolean string true or false.")
event "Built-in and" : literal("and(p,q) returns true exactly when both canonical Boolean arguments are true.")
event "Built-in or" : literal("or(p,q) returns true when at least one canonical Boolean argument is true.")
event "Built-in select" : literal("select(p,a,b) constructively chooses a when p is true and b when p is false.")
event "Built-in assert equal" : literal("assert_equal(a,b) returns a only when a and b are exact equals; otherwise compilation stops.")
event "Instruction array 6" : literal("Semantic instructions contain semantic_triple.")
event "Built-in semantic triple" : literal("semantic_triple(subject,predicate,object) returns canonical text in the form subject <predicate> object.")
event "Instruction array 7" : literal("Sequential-ID instructions are sequential_encode, sequential_decode, and sequential_verify.")
event "Built-in sequential encode" : literal("sequential_encode(x,A) ranks x in shortlex order over ordered alphabet A and returns an arbitrary-precision decimal ID.")
event "Built-in sequential decode" : literal("sequential_decode(N,A) un-ranks decimal ID N over alphabet A and returns its unique finite string.")
event "Built-in sequential verify" : literal("sequential_verify(x,A) returns true only when decoding the encoding of x is byte-for-byte x.")
event "Instruction array 8" : literal("Memory instructions are backward reference, map_coordinate, automatic event capture, and automatic square-map construction.")
event "Built-in map coordinate" : literal("map_coordinate(i,n) returns row,column for zero-based event index i in the least square map containing n events.")
event "Automatic event capture" : literal("After evaluation, the compiler constructs metadata, computes an ID, proves the reverse, and emits one immutable event object.")
event "Automatic square map" : literal("Events are placed row-major in the least side by side square; remaining cells are explicit null vacancies.")
event "Shortlex encode step 1" : literal("Validate UTF-8, alphabet uniqueness, alphabet size 2 through 1024, and value length at most 4096 symbols.")
event "Shortlex encode step 2" : literal("Return decimal zero for the empty value.")
event "Shortlex encode step 3" : literal("Let base b be the number of ordered alphabet symbols.")
event "Shortlex encode step 4" : literal("Compute the shorter-string count S as the sum of b to powers 1 through n minus 1.")
event "Shortlex encode step 5" : literal("Map each value symbol to its zero-based alphabet digit and reject any absent symbol.")
event "Shortlex encode step 6" : literal("Fold digits left with rank = rank times b plus digit.")
event "Shortlex encode step 7" : literal("Return sequential ID = S plus rank plus one as a normalized decimal string.")
event "Shortlex decode step 1" : literal("Normalize the non-negative decimal ID and return empty for zero.")
event "Shortlex decode step 2" : literal("Set remaining to ID, length to one, and current bucket size to b.")
event "Shortlex decode step 3" : literal("While remaining exceeds the bucket, subtract the bucket, increment length, and multiply the bucket by b.")
event "Shortlex decode step 4" : literal("Set the zero-based within-bucket offset to remaining minus one.")
event "Shortlex decode step 5" : literal("Allocate length result positions initialized to the first alphabet symbol.")
event "Shortlex decode step 6" : literal("From last position to first, divide offset by b and use each remainder as the alphabet digit.")
event "Shortlex decode step 7" : literal("Join the symbols and require exact byte equality with the original value before event emission.")
event "Bijection proof" : literal("Disjoint length buckets plus fixed-width base-b positional ranking make encode and decode mutual inverses.")
event "Compiler UTF-8 component" : literal("utf8Symbols validates leading bytes, continuation bytes, scalar range, surrogate exclusion, and overlong encodings.")
event "Compiler big-natural normalize" : literal("natural::normalize validates decimal digits and removes insignificant leading zeros.")
event "Compiler big-natural compare" : literal("natural::compare orders normalized decimals by length and then lexicographically.")
event "Compiler big-natural add" : literal("natural::add performs right-to-left decimal addition with carry.")
event "Compiler big-natural subtract" : literal("natural::subtract performs checked non-negative decimal subtraction with borrow.")
event "Compiler big-natural multiply" : literal("natural::multiply and multiplySmall perform arbitrary-precision decimal multiplication.")
event "Compiler big-natural division" : literal("natural::divide and divideSmall perform long division and return exact quotient-remainder pairs.")
event "Compiler signed integer component" : literal("BigInteger stores a sign and normalized natural magnitude; helpers implement signed add, multiply, divide, and modulo.")
event "Compiler Shortlex component" : literal("Shortlex validates alphabets and implements the same rank and un-rank algorithms as PHP SequentialStringId.")
event "Compiler diagnostic component" : literal("Diagnostic attaches physical line and column to syntax and semantic failures.")
event "Compiler lexer component" : literal("Lexer recognizes identifiers, escaped UTF-8 strings, signed decimals, $n references, punctuation, and end of line.")
event "Compiler parser component" : literal("Parser enforces one event statement per line and builds recursive expression trees with an optional event alphabet.")
event "Compiler evaluator component" : literal("evaluate resolves earlier event values, evaluates nested expressions inside-out, checks arity, and dispatches built-ins.")
event "Compiler container component" : literal("containerize and decontainerize implement and validate the GPDB1 length-prefixed UTF-8 container format.")
event "Compiler event ID component" : literal("eventId combines physical line and deterministic FNV-1a source hash into a stable gpil event ID.")
event "Compiler timestamp component" : literal("isoTimestamp emits UTC ISO 8601 timestamps with millisecond precision.")
event "Compiler JSON component" : literal("jsonEscape and writeDatabase serialize exact UTF-8 values, proof data, instruction metadata, and complete map cells.")
event "Compiler pipeline component" : literal("parseProgram, compile, and main coordinate input, transactional compilation, output, exit codes, and summary diagnostics.")
event "Compiler self-test component" : literal("selfTest checks known base-2 shortlex ordinals, containers, references, arithmetic, and exact assertions.")
event "PHP bootstrap component" : literal("src/bootstrap.php loads BigNatural, SequentialStringId, EventStore, and DatabaseReportPdf in dependency order.")
event "PHP BigNatural normalize" : literal("BigNatural::normalize validates and canonicalizes non-negative decimal strings.")
event "PHP BigNatural compare" : literal("BigNatural::compare orders arbitrary-precision decimal strings without native integer conversion.")
event "PHP BigNatural add" : literal("BigNatural::add and addSmall implement decimal addition with carry.")
event "PHP BigNatural subtract" : literal("BigNatural::subtract implements checked decimal subtraction with borrow.")
event "PHP BigNatural multiply" : literal("BigNatural::multiplySmall multiplies a decimal string by a bounded native factor.")
event "PHP BigNatural divide" : literal("BigNatural::divideSmall returns a normalized decimal quotient and native remainder.")
event "PHP SequentialStringId constructor" : literal("SequentialStringId::__construct validates UTF-8, uniqueness, and the 2 through 1024 symbol alphabet bounds.")
event "PHP SequentialStringId encode" : literal("SequentialStringId::encode performs arbitrary-precision shortlex ranking with a 4096 symbol context limit.")
event "PHP SequentialStringId decode" : literal("SequentialStringId::decode locates the length bucket and performs repeated base division to reconstruct the value.")
event "PHP SequentialStringId proof" : literal("SequentialStringId::encodeVerified emits an ID only after decode of that ID exactly equals the original input.")
event "PHP EventStore constructor" : literal("EventStore::__construct creates the data directory and initial JSON state when required.")
event "PHP EventStore read" : literal("EventStore::read uses a shared file lock, decodes JSON, and rebuilds derived square-map metadata.")
event "PHP EventStore append" : literal("EventStore::append uses an exclusive lock, appends one verified node, rebuilds the map, truncates, writes, and flushes atomically.")
event "PHP EventStore square map" : literal("EventStore::buildSquareMap computes the least square, row-major cells, and total, occupied, and vacant metrics.")
event "PHP EventStore timestamp" : literal("EventStore::timestamp returns a UTC ISO 8601 timestamp with millisecond precision.")
event "PHP EventStore decoder" : literal("EventStore::decodeState rejects invalid JSON structures, preserves top-level manifests, and refreshes derived map data.")
event "PHP API GET" : literal("api.php GET returns database state and compiler limits; export-report returns the current complete PDF snapshot.")
event "PHP API POST" : literal("api.php POST validates JSON create-event input, ranks and proves the value, constructs all required fields, and commits it.")
event "PHP API payload built-ins" : literal("readPayload uses content type checks, file_get_contents, json_decode, and JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR for strict request parsing.")
event "PHP API event ID built-ins" : literal("createEventId uses microtime, floor, base_convert, random_bytes, bin2hex, and sprintf for collision-resistant runtime IDs.")
event "PHP API native integer metric" : literal("isNativeInteger compares decimal digit length and lexicographic order with PHP_INT_MAX without lossy conversion.")
event "PHP PDF report builder" : literal("DatabaseReportPdf traverses every top-level property, map cell, and recursively flattened field of every event.")
event "PHP PDF layout engine" : literal("Page, title, section, paragraph, field, wrap, drawing, and continuation helpers create consistent paginated A4 output.")
event "PHP PDF Unicode preservation" : literal("asciiSafe represents non-ASCII scalar values as explicit U+ notation when standard PDF fonts cannot encode them.")
event "PHP PDF serializer" : literal("compilePdf writes PDF 1.4 objects, content streams, fonts, pages, xref offsets, metadata, page numbers, and EOF trailer.")
event "PHP web entry component" : literal("index.php supplies security headers and the Memory Square form, proof output, map modes, search, canvas, and report export control.")
event "JavaScript API component" : literal("assets/app.js loads state, posts create-event JSON, displays server errors, and renders every database response.")
event "JavaScript map component" : literal("InfiniteMemoryMap builds node positions from cells and implements high-DPI resize, fit, center, pan, zoom, hit testing, and drawing.")
event "JavaScript search component" : literal("renderSearch matches label, value, event ID, sequential ID, and timestamp and opens complete node details.")
event "Template compiler guidance" : literal("template/compiler.html contributes character-map loading, base conversion, encode, decode, frequency, preview, and C syntax display patterns.")
event "System source inventory" : literal("Constructive artifacts are compiler source and binary, docs, examples, PHP classes, api.php, index.php, assets, tests, and tools.")
event "Database schema" : literal("memory-event-node/2.0 stores full reversible event evidence and a complete least-square row-major memory map.")
event "Report completeness" : literal("report.pdf includes schema, update time, map dimensions and occupancy, every map cell, every event field, and all compiler and PHP component events.")
